1
00:00:02,045 --> 00:00:03,786
[dance music playing]

2
00:00:15,406 --> 00:00:18,279
[indistinct chattering]

3
00:00:23,153 --> 00:00:24,589
[clink]

4
00:00:26,417 --> 00:00:29,029
[indistinct chattering]

5
00:00:32,206 --> 00:00:33,163
Omar.

6
00:00:36,253 --> 00:00:37,211
Hey.

7
00:00:39,213 --> 00:00:41,911
[both laugh]

8
00:00:52,791 --> 00:00:55,359
[dance music]

9
00:01:06,979 --> 00:01:08,024
[Yoli]
'Excuse me.'

10
00:01:15,379 --> 00:01:17,512
Excuse...Hey.
Muvete, idiota!

11
00:01:17,599 --> 00:01:18,643
Let me go!

12
00:01:31,787 --> 00:01:33,136
[heel scrapes]

13
00:01:33,223 --> 00:01:34,659
- What are you, blind?
-I'm sorry.

14
00:01:43,277 --> 00:01:45,235
[cell phone buzzing]

15
00:01:50,980 --> 00:01:52,590
[phone snaps shut]

16
00:01:52,677 --> 00:01:54,201
[keys jangle]

17
00:01:59,510 --> 00:02:02,122
[police radio chatter]

18
00:02:04,428 --> 00:02:07,039
[siren blaring]

19
00:02:16,614 --> 00:02:20,531
Ah. You look, uh,
marginally rested.

20
00:02:20,618 --> 00:02:23,143
I was hoping I'd actually
get to REM. Sleep tonight.

21
00:02:23,230 --> 00:02:25,928
There's another detective here.
Maybe you can go back to bed.

22
00:02:26,015 --> 00:02:28,191
That's weird. Sac PD called
for help on this.

23
00:02:28,278 --> 00:02:29,584
You two CBI?

24
00:02:29,671 --> 00:02:32,413
Yeah, I'm Teresa Lisbon.
This is Patrick Jane.

25
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:35,372
Sergeant Henderson. Just holding
down the scene till you arrived.

26
00:02:35,459 --> 00:02:37,331
I was in the neighborhood.

27
00:02:37,418 --> 00:02:40,377
Two shots to the head.
No purse or ID on the victim.

28
00:02:40,464 --> 00:02:42,249
The car's registered
to a Yolanda Herrera.

29
00:02:42,336 --> 00:02:43,772
[Lisbon]
'Any witnesses?'

30
00:02:43,859 --> 00:02:46,209
No, but these officers
responded to an anonymous tip

31
00:02:46,296 --> 00:02:48,690
so somebody
had to see something.

32
00:02:48,777 --> 00:02:52,433
It's from, uh, Luxure. It's
a, uh, club down the street.

33
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:54,261
She wouldn't be
the first club head

34
00:02:54,348 --> 00:02:56,088
I've seen done
in by her dealer.

35
00:02:56,176 --> 00:02:59,744
I applaud your certainty but I
don't think it's cut and dried.

36
00:02:59,831 --> 00:03:03,922
She got the clothes right,
look at her hands. Short nails.

37
00:03:04,009 --> 00:03:05,576
very sloppy paint job.

38
00:03:05,663 --> 00:03:07,404
[Lisbon]
'Maybe she was in a rush.'

39
00:03:07,491 --> 00:03:09,363
Doubtful. Free pass
to the champagne room

40
00:03:09,450 --> 00:03:12,975
requires very careful
attention to detail.

41
00:03:13,062 --> 00:03:14,759
You gotta be joking, huh?

42
00:03:14,846 --> 00:03:17,327
I work these streets.
I know a club girl.

43
00:03:17,414 --> 00:03:19,460
Apparently not, because you
missed a small bruise

44
00:03:19,547 --> 00:03:22,289
on her left ankle. I'm guessing
she turned her ankle

45
00:03:22,376 --> 00:03:23,986
trying to walk
in these shoes.

46
00:03:24,073 --> 00:03:25,770
And her arms
are very well muscled.

47
00:03:25,857 --> 00:03:28,469
Lisbon, correct me
if I'm wrong--

48
00:03:28,556 --> 00:03:32,560
that appears to be
a sports bra she's wearing.

49
00:03:32,647 --> 00:03:34,866
- I don't know. Probably.
- What are you getting at?

50
00:03:34,953 --> 00:03:37,304
Well, your club girl here
was in a disguise--

51
00:03:37,391 --> 00:03:39,697
A tomboy
trying to blend in.

52
00:03:39,784 --> 00:03:42,265
The question is why?

53
00:03:42,352 --> 00:03:43,919
And what was her game?

54
00:03:44,006 --> 00:03:46,182
Is this really productive?

55
00:03:46,269 --> 00:03:47,357
You knew her.

56
00:03:47,444 --> 00:03:49,577
No, I didn't.

57
00:03:49,664 --> 00:03:51,840
Your voice just pitched
a little higher like when

58
00:03:51,927 --> 00:03:53,885
[Jane]
'you said you happened
to be around.'

59
00:03:53,972 --> 00:03:56,061
Is he right?
Did you know the victim?

60
00:03:56,148 --> 00:03:57,585
Of course not.
That's ridiculous.

61
00:03:57,672 --> 00:04:01,632
Aha! I know who this woman--
this--this woman here--

62
00:04:01,719 --> 00:04:02,677
okay. I'm here.

63
00:04:02,764 --> 00:04:04,461
Hey, what the hell
is going on?

64
00:04:04,548 --> 00:04:06,376
Yolanda Herrera
is an undercover cop.

65
00:04:06,463 --> 00:04:08,160
That's exactly
what I was gonna say.

66
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:10,250
Yeah, big whoop for you,
smart ass.

67
00:04:10,337 --> 00:04:13,688
No one can know that. It'll be
more dangerous for the next cop.

68
00:04:13,775 --> 00:04:15,777
You're not known for
your management skills.

69
00:04:15,864 --> 00:04:18,301
Work the case.
I'll help you where I can.

70
00:04:18,388 --> 00:04:21,478
But Yoli's identity
must remain confidential.

71
00:04:21,565 --> 00:04:23,828
And keep this circus act
under control, got it?

72
00:04:23,915 --> 00:04:25,439
Got it. Yeah.

73
00:04:25,526 --> 00:04:27,397
Wha--

74
00:04:27,484 --> 00:04:30,095
Disappointing, Lisbon. I thought
you might push back a little.

75
00:04:30,182 --> 00:04:32,446
Guy called me
a "circus act."

76
00:04:32,533 --> 00:04:35,187
Hey. The man is grieving.
You push back.

77
00:04:35,275 --> 00:04:36,711
- Okay, I will.
- Don't you dare.

78
00:04:36,798 --> 00:04:39,191
- Okay. Said that I could.
- I take it back.

79
00:04:39,279 --> 00:04:40,541
- Alright.
- Okay?

80
00:04:40,628 --> 00:04:42,412
[inhales deeply]

81
00:04:42,499 --> 00:04:43,674
I need a little rest.

82
00:04:45,546 --> 00:04:47,678
[theme music]

83
00:04:56,252 --> 00:04:57,209
[Officer]
'Yolanda Concepcion
was her real name'

84
00:04:57,297 --> 00:04:58,776
but everyone
called her "Yoli."

85
00:04:58,863 --> 00:05:01,388
She leaves behind a family--
Husband, two young children.

86
00:05:01,475 --> 00:05:04,869
She's a valuable member
of my narcotics task force.

87
00:05:04,956 --> 00:05:06,654
What was she doing
out here tonight?

88
00:05:06,741 --> 00:05:08,177
She's supposed to be
getting friendly

89
00:05:08,264 --> 00:05:10,092
with a dealer named Omar Vega.

90
00:05:10,179 --> 00:05:12,529
He's a major player here
in South Sac.

91
00:05:12,616 --> 00:05:14,966
We think his crew
is behind a

92
00:05:15,053 --> 00:05:16,707
recent rise
in crime around here.

93
00:05:16,794 --> 00:05:19,710
- You think Vega made her cover?
- Too early to tell.

94
00:05:19,797 --> 00:05:22,844
But he's popped people for a lot
less than being undercover cops.

95
00:05:22,931 --> 00:05:26,326
Okay. We'll start
at the club. Thanks.

96
00:05:26,413 --> 00:05:29,285
Jane, meet me at Luxure.

97
00:05:29,372 --> 00:05:30,765
[rock music]

98
00:05:30,852 --> 00:05:32,332
What?

99
00:05:32,419 --> 00:05:33,376
I can't hear you!

100
00:05:35,378 --> 00:05:37,511
Still can't hear you!

101
00:05:37,598 --> 00:05:40,252
Bye!

102
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:42,603
[rock music]

103
00:05:51,481 --> 00:05:53,831
- Jane!
- Oh, hey, Lisbon!

104
00:05:53,918 --> 00:05:56,965
Meet Vince Candide. He's our
host. He's a womanizing buffoon

105
00:05:57,052 --> 00:05:59,228
but I think you'll be
amused by his presumption.

106
00:05:59,315 --> 00:06:01,186
- What?
- Huh?

107
00:06:01,273 --> 00:06:02,405
He..

108
00:06:02,492 --> 00:06:04,581
This is...he..

109
00:06:04,668 --> 00:06:06,148
Have you seen this woman?

110
00:06:08,237 --> 00:06:10,239
What about Omar Vega?

111
00:06:10,326 --> 00:06:11,283
Who?

112
00:06:11,371 --> 00:06:13,764
[both]
Omar Vega!

113
00:06:13,851 --> 00:06:15,940
Sorry. I gotta go run the place.

114
00:06:16,027 --> 00:06:18,639
He can't hear!

115
00:06:18,726 --> 00:06:19,683
Thanks, Vince!

116
00:06:25,733 --> 00:06:27,865
If Vega's here,
he's over there.

117
00:06:31,434 --> 00:06:32,392
[Jane]
'Thank you.'

118
00:06:35,786 --> 00:06:37,788
Ah, that's more like it.

119
00:06:37,875 --> 00:06:40,356
Pardon me,
have you seen Omar Vega?

120
00:06:40,443 --> 00:06:42,402
You're never gonna
find him like that.

121
00:06:44,316 --> 00:06:45,535
What do we got here?

122
00:06:45,622 --> 00:06:46,971
[feedback whines]

123
00:06:48,973 --> 00:06:51,367
Ladies and gentlemen,
thank you for your attention.

124
00:06:51,454 --> 00:06:53,717
My colleague over there

125
00:06:53,804 --> 00:06:56,154
in her not-here-to-party
clothes

126
00:06:56,241 --> 00:06:57,678
is five-o.

127
00:06:57,765 --> 00:06:58,983
Yeah, CBI.

128
00:06:59,070 --> 00:07:01,029
She's looking for Omar Vega.

129
00:07:01,116 --> 00:07:04,946
I have $500 in this pocket
for whoever can point him out.

130
00:07:05,033 --> 00:07:08,645
That's 500 big ones
just to use your pointy finger.

131
00:07:08,732 --> 00:07:11,605
And then we'll take it
from there.

132
00:07:11,692 --> 00:07:13,128
Thank you. Party on.

133
00:07:13,781 --> 00:07:15,043
Subtle.

134
00:07:15,130 --> 00:07:17,567
But effective.
He's over by the bar.

135
00:07:17,654 --> 00:07:20,396
[indistinct chattering]

136
00:07:20,483 --> 00:07:22,180
You're someone nobody
wants to look at

137
00:07:22,267 --> 00:07:24,748
so I'm guessing
you're Mr. Vega.

138
00:07:24,835 --> 00:07:25,880
I like your swagger.

139
00:07:25,967 --> 00:07:26,968
Well, thank you.

140
00:07:28,622 --> 00:07:29,797
We're investigating
a murder.

141
00:07:29,884 --> 00:07:32,103
No need.
I know what Yoli looks like.

142
00:07:32,190 --> 00:07:34,323
I hear she got popped. Shame.

143
00:07:34,410 --> 00:07:36,630
Was Yoli
at the club tonight?

144
00:07:36,717 --> 00:07:40,024
You know the answer to that,
or you wouldn't be here.

145
00:07:40,111 --> 00:07:42,766
- Did you talk to her?
- Yeah. Maybe.

146
00:07:42,853 --> 00:07:45,813
- What did you talk about?
- Foolishness.

147
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:47,554
She's just another haina
from the neighborhood

148
00:07:47,641 --> 00:07:49,730
trying to get my attention.

149
00:07:49,817 --> 00:07:50,818
Hmm.

150
00:07:50,905 --> 00:07:52,950
And did she
get your attention?

151
00:07:53,037 --> 00:07:54,212
Did you take her outside?

152
00:07:54,299 --> 00:07:55,910
No, ma'am, I did not.

153
00:07:55,997 --> 00:07:59,914
I've been here all night.
Please, ask around.

154
00:08:00,001 --> 00:08:02,699
No need.
He's telling the truth.

155
00:08:02,786 --> 00:08:04,222
I've got nothing to hide.

156
00:08:04,309 --> 00:08:06,529
Well, that's not
entirely true.

157
00:08:06,616 --> 00:08:09,097
You're hiding
profound anger.

158
00:08:09,184 --> 00:08:10,402
Is that right?

159
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:12,709
Mm. Mm-hmm.

160
00:08:14,755 --> 00:08:16,974
The tension in your jawline
gives it away.

161
00:08:18,715 --> 00:08:20,587
[Jane]
'What is it
that's bothering you?'

162
00:08:20,674 --> 00:08:23,111
It's not a woman.
I don't think you care enough.

163
00:08:23,198 --> 00:08:26,462
Not global warming.
What is it you covet most?

164
00:08:26,549 --> 00:08:28,943
Money? No.

165
00:08:29,030 --> 00:08:30,814
Respect.

166
00:08:30,901 --> 00:08:34,601
This is a question
of respect.

167
00:08:34,688 --> 00:08:36,690
Someone disrespected you,
didn't they?

168
00:08:36,777 --> 00:08:38,822
How? What did they do
to you?

169
00:08:38,909 --> 00:08:41,912
Keep guessing, pinstripes.

170
00:08:41,999 --> 00:08:43,610
Pinstripes.Ma'am..

171
00:08:43,697 --> 00:08:45,046
Are we done?

172
00:08:45,133 --> 00:08:46,874
Yes, we're done, sir.

173
00:08:51,966 --> 00:08:52,967
Whew.

174
00:08:54,795 --> 00:08:55,926
Interesting.

175
00:08:56,013 --> 00:08:57,711
Yeah.

176
00:08:57,798 --> 00:09:00,148
I like the "pinstripes."

177
00:09:00,235 --> 00:09:03,499
Vega took control of South Sac
in less than a year.

178
00:09:03,586 --> 00:09:05,806
His competitors didn't agree
to work with him...

179
00:09:05,893 --> 00:09:07,111
..they ended up like this.

180
00:09:07,198 --> 00:09:09,157
Yeah, I see how
that could be persuasive.

181
00:09:09,244 --> 00:09:10,375
No criminal record?

182
00:09:10,462 --> 00:09:12,508
Vega's brutal and smart.

183
00:09:12,595 --> 00:09:14,466
Always one step
ahead of us.

184
00:09:14,554 --> 00:09:16,860
Ran his organization
like a terror cell.

185
00:09:16,947 --> 00:09:19,384
Everyone knows what they
need to get the job done.

186
00:09:19,471 --> 00:09:22,170
So his hands stay clean.
What was Yoli's assignment?

187
00:09:22,257 --> 00:09:25,216
To find Vega's current base of
operation. It's always changing.

188
00:09:25,303 --> 00:09:27,262
We've got our work
cut out for us.

189
00:09:27,349 --> 00:09:29,612
- Where are we with suspects?
- None we can find.

190
00:09:29,699 --> 00:09:32,136
I've a copy of the 9-1-1 call,
from a payphone

191
00:09:32,223 --> 00:09:34,835
three blocks away
from the crime scene.

192
00:09:34,922 --> 00:09:36,967
[woman on tape recorder
'9-1-1, what's your emergency?'

193
00:09:37,054 --> 00:09:39,143
[Summer]
'Um, yeah, there's a dead chick'

194
00:09:39,230 --> 00:09:41,581
on Kennon near 4th
in case you're interested.

195
00:09:41,668 --> 00:09:43,060
Are there cameras
near that phone?

196
00:09:43,147 --> 00:09:44,627
None.

197
00:09:44,714 --> 00:09:46,890
Got a hit on the victims
missing credit cards.

198
00:09:46,977 --> 00:09:49,066
Room charge, this
morning at a downtown hotel.

199
00:09:49,153 --> 00:09:52,461
Take Rigsby. Yoli's cell phone
was missing, too, right?

200
00:09:52,548 --> 00:09:54,550
Yeah, but the carrier hasn't
received a signal

201
00:09:54,637 --> 00:09:56,508
since last night.
Whoever took the phone

202
00:09:56,596 --> 00:09:58,249
powered it down
or pulled the battery.

203
00:09:58,336 --> 00:09:59,511
Stay on it.

204
00:10:01,296 --> 00:10:03,777
- You talked to the family yet?
- I'm headed there now.

205
00:10:03,864 --> 00:10:05,735
What do they know
about Yoli's assignment?

206
00:10:05,822 --> 00:10:08,433
Nothing. It's an ongoing
investigation, so they can't.

207
00:10:08,520 --> 00:10:09,609
Understood.

208
00:10:12,524 --> 00:10:16,137
[Lolo]
'I told her not to get involved
in this undercover crap.'

209
00:10:16,224 --> 00:10:18,443
Desk jobs have benefits.
They pay good enough.

210
00:10:19,923 --> 00:10:22,143
It was one of these
drug dealers, wasn't it?

211
00:10:22,230 --> 00:10:24,711
I'm afraid I can't talk
about that now.

212
00:10:24,798 --> 00:10:28,453
Still? Are you kidding me? What
does it matter now? My wife's--

213
00:10:28,540 --> 00:10:30,455
[Jane]
'She's the greatest mother
in the world.'

214
00:10:38,725 --> 00:10:40,161
Hello there.

215
00:10:40,248 --> 00:10:43,643
Who is it? Hi.

216
00:10:43,730 --> 00:10:45,035
Rafi?

217
00:10:45,122 --> 00:10:46,733
[Elvia]
Rafi? Rafi?

218
00:10:48,430 --> 00:10:51,825
Oh, there you are. I got him.
Sorry about that, Lalo.

219
00:10:51,912 --> 00:10:54,088
This is Elvia, Yoli's cousin.

220
00:10:54,175 --> 00:10:57,178
She moved in a couple months ago
to help with the kids.

221
00:10:57,265 --> 00:10:58,440
He's a beautiful boy.

222
00:10:58,527 --> 00:11:01,182
[Rafi babbling]

223
00:11:01,269 --> 00:11:02,313
He doesn't know yet.

224
00:11:05,099 --> 00:11:08,450
How do you tell a little kid
he won't see his mom again?

225
00:11:08,537 --> 00:11:10,495
Did she talk to you
about her work?

226
00:11:10,582 --> 00:11:16,327
No. But I barely knew what Yoli
was doing on a daily basis.

227
00:11:16,414 --> 00:11:18,721
I'm sorry.
Why are we doing this?

228
00:11:18,808 --> 00:11:21,158
To bring your wife's
murder to justice.

229
00:11:21,245 --> 00:11:23,030
For you and your family.

230
00:11:23,117 --> 00:11:24,031
Justice?

231
00:11:25,510 --> 00:11:27,295
You think
my kids are gonna care

232
00:11:27,382 --> 00:11:30,515
when some crack dealer
goes down for this?

233
00:11:30,602 --> 00:11:34,650
They lost their mother.
I lost my wife.

234
00:11:34,737 --> 00:11:36,652
For what?

235
00:11:36,739 --> 00:11:37,871
War on drugs?

236
00:11:41,875 --> 00:11:42,963
Give me a break.

237
00:11:46,227 --> 00:11:48,533
[humming]

238
00:11:48,620 --> 00:11:50,622
[pot bubbling]

239
00:11:52,494 --> 00:11:53,756
Mm!

240
00:11:53,843 --> 00:11:56,585
- 'That's a nice tune.'
- Oh! Ooh.

241
00:11:56,672 --> 00:11:59,457
Didn't mean to startle you.
I'm sorry. What--what's cooking?

242
00:11:59,544 --> 00:12:01,808
Spaghetti.
It's for the kids' lunch.

243
00:12:01,895 --> 00:12:03,200
Ah.

244
00:12:03,287 --> 00:12:05,333
You and Yoli must have
been very close

245
00:12:05,420 --> 00:12:07,509
to help out
with the family like this.

246
00:12:08,902 --> 00:12:11,034
Yeah. We were like sisters.

247
00:12:11,121 --> 00:12:13,907
Really? I don't think so.

248
00:12:13,994 --> 00:12:14,951
What?

249
00:12:15,038 --> 00:12:16,431
The humming.

250
00:12:16,518 --> 00:12:18,520
I hum. So what?

251
00:12:18,607 --> 00:12:21,523
Well, humming--
it's like comfort food.

252
00:12:21,610 --> 00:12:23,264
Takes us back to the breast.

253
00:12:23,351 --> 00:12:26,049
And you are the mom
of the family now, aren't you?

254
00:12:27,834 --> 00:12:29,531
Deep down,
you're glad she's dead.

255
00:12:29,618 --> 00:12:32,882
What the hell
kind of cop are you?

256
00:12:32,969 --> 00:12:34,623
Jane? What's going on?

257
00:12:34,710 --> 00:12:37,191
I was about to ask Elvia what
she was doing

258
00:12:37,278 --> 00:12:38,496
at Luxure last night.

259
00:12:40,629 --> 00:12:44,676
The faded stamp on your wrist.
I have one just like it.

260
00:12:44,764 --> 00:12:46,461
You followed Yoli
while she was working?

261
00:12:46,548 --> 00:12:49,377
Elvia, what were you thinking?
I swear, if you did anything

262
00:12:49,464 --> 00:12:50,421
to get her killed..

263
00:12:50,508 --> 00:12:51,596
Why'd you follow her?

264
00:12:51,683 --> 00:12:55,731
Uh, she has
a little thing for Lalo.

265
00:12:55,818 --> 00:12:56,950
What--what are you
talking about?

266
00:12:58,081 --> 00:12:59,387
I think she should explain.

267
00:13:03,565 --> 00:13:05,915
Yoli didn't deserve you.

268
00:13:06,002 --> 00:13:08,483
Look, I-I..

269
00:13:08,570 --> 00:13:12,400
what I found in her jeans when
I was washing more than once.

270
00:13:12,487 --> 00:13:14,097
Condoms. Yoli was on the pill.

271
00:13:14,184 --> 00:13:17,144
I went to the club to see
who she was sleeping with.

272
00:13:17,231 --> 00:13:18,798
- What did you see?
- Nothing.

273
00:13:18,885 --> 00:13:21,322
I--she was in a rush
to get out of there

274
00:13:21,409 --> 00:13:23,280
and texting somebody,
but I lost her.

275
00:13:23,367 --> 00:13:27,328
We'll need you to come to the
office, make a full statement.

276
00:13:27,415 --> 00:13:29,591
Might as well pack
your things before you go.

277
00:13:31,071 --> 00:13:33,029
You're not coming back
in this house.

278
00:13:33,116 --> 00:13:34,814
B-but...

279
00:13:34,901 --> 00:13:36,424
I went there for you, Lalo!

280
00:13:40,254 --> 00:13:42,256
Whoa.

281
00:13:42,343 --> 00:13:44,736
Little more salt,
but that's pretty good.

282
00:13:44,824 --> 00:13:46,086
Kids are gonna love that.

283
00:13:49,437 --> 00:13:52,135
A charge was made, this morning
from a stolen credit card.

284
00:13:52,222 --> 00:13:53,920
Let me guess--
husband on the prowl?

285
00:13:54,007 --> 00:13:55,617
Killer on the run.

286
00:13:55,704 --> 00:13:56,661
Oh.

287
00:13:57,924 --> 00:13:59,360
[man #1]
'Uh, here we go.'

288
00:13:59,447 --> 00:14:01,318
'One American breakfast,
three bloody marys'

289
00:14:01,405 --> 00:14:03,712
delivered to room 618.

290
00:14:03,799 --> 00:14:04,844
- Thank you.
- Mm-hmm.

291
00:14:11,111 --> 00:14:12,112
[man #2]
Who's there?

292
00:14:12,199 --> 00:14:13,504
Police. Open the door.

293
00:14:13,591 --> 00:14:14,766
Just a minute!

294
00:14:14,854 --> 00:14:16,246
[thud]

295
00:14:16,333 --> 00:14:17,421
[beep]

296
00:14:18,988 --> 00:14:19,989
Please don't shoot.

297
00:14:21,948 --> 00:14:23,819
[groans]
I got it.

298
00:14:23,906 --> 00:14:25,038
[Rigsby]
'Get up. Come on.'

299
00:14:26,648 --> 00:14:29,129
can you pass me
a hand towel?

300
00:14:29,216 --> 00:14:30,826
Step out of
the bathroom, please.

301
00:14:30,913 --> 00:14:33,350
I swear to God, I've never seen
that woman before.

302
00:14:33,437 --> 00:14:36,397
Oh, shush. Put that thing away.
What are you, a maniac?

303
00:14:36,484 --> 00:14:37,964
You could hurt someone.

304
00:14:44,448 --> 00:14:47,364
[Cho]
So, Summer, I need you to tell
me why you were making charges

305
00:14:47,451 --> 00:14:49,192
on a murder victim's
credit card

306
00:14:49,279 --> 00:14:50,977
hours after her death.

307
00:14:51,064 --> 00:14:52,674
Cho...

308
00:14:52,761 --> 00:14:54,806
that's Korean, right?

309
00:14:54,894 --> 00:14:57,548
I also need you to explain
how you got that card.

310
00:14:57,635 --> 00:14:58,767
Bad back, huh?

311
00:15:00,290 --> 00:15:01,291
Yeah.

312
00:15:01,378 --> 00:15:02,989
I can tell.

313
00:15:03,076 --> 00:15:06,253
Is there anything I can do
to make it any better?

314
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:07,950
No.

315
00:15:08,037 --> 00:15:11,127
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

316
00:15:11,214 --> 00:15:14,304
Look, I don't know anything
about any dead chick.

317
00:15:16,089 --> 00:15:17,742
[click]

318
00:15:17,829 --> 00:15:20,136
[woman on tape recorder]
'Yeah, there's a dead chick'

319
00:15:20,223 --> 00:15:22,182
on Kennon near 4th in case you're interested.

320
00:15:22,269 --> 00:15:23,705
[laughs]

321
00:15:25,489 --> 00:15:27,143
Wow! You're way more slick

322
00:15:27,230 --> 00:15:29,189
than the trolls that
usually bust my butt.

323
00:15:29,276 --> 00:15:30,712
- Did you shoot the victim?
- No!

324
00:15:30,799 --> 00:15:32,322
Did you see who did?

325
00:15:32,409 --> 00:15:35,108
I heard shots. I ran to help.
She was already dead.

326
00:15:35,195 --> 00:15:36,631
At least I called it in.

327
00:15:36,718 --> 00:15:38,154
You ran to help?

328
00:15:38,241 --> 00:15:40,374
Why wouldn't I?
Poor thing.

329
00:15:40,461 --> 00:15:42,158
You took the victim's
credit cards.

330
00:15:45,509 --> 00:15:47,294
This is about Omar Vega,
isn't it?

331
00:15:50,166 --> 00:15:51,994
What do you know
about Vega?

332
00:15:52,081 --> 00:15:53,691
Hmm.

333
00:15:53,778 --> 00:15:56,259
I know that your dead girl
was hanging with him.

334
00:15:56,346 --> 00:15:59,567
I also know that I've an 18-hour
window with a stolen card,

335
00:15:59,654 --> 00:16:02,309
but you made it there
in record time.

336
00:16:02,396 --> 00:16:03,527
You're after someone big.

337
00:16:04,441 --> 00:16:05,442
Ahem.

338
00:16:05,529 --> 00:16:07,575
Look, I know things.

339
00:16:08,968 --> 00:16:10,534
Maybe we could make a deal.

340
00:16:10,621 --> 00:16:12,275
- What do you got?
- What's your deal?

341
00:16:16,192 --> 00:16:18,586
You give me something useful,
I'll drop the theft charge.

342
00:16:19,717 --> 00:16:20,849
Pinkie swear?

343
00:16:22,416 --> 00:16:23,330
Fine.

344
00:16:24,853 --> 00:16:26,986
Vega just got his ass
handed to him.

345
00:16:27,073 --> 00:16:30,032
The Perry Boys raided his
stash house a couple days ago.

346
00:16:30,119 --> 00:16:32,078
- Cleaned out all his coke.
- How much?

347
00:16:32,165 --> 00:16:33,731
Like ten keys, maybe more.

348
00:16:36,125 --> 00:16:38,954
- The Perry Boys?
- Yeah. The Perry Boys.

349
00:16:40,521 --> 00:16:43,567
Vega needs more product
and revenge fast,

350
00:16:43,654 --> 00:16:45,917
or else his customers
are gonna be lost

351
00:16:46,005 --> 00:16:48,616
and, uh,
he'll lose respect.

352
00:16:48,703 --> 00:16:52,098
I bet you just doodle
in that thing, don't you?

353
00:16:52,185 --> 00:16:53,360
[chuckles]

354
00:16:55,492 --> 00:16:59,888
So. That's enough to
get me out of here, right?

355
00:16:59,975 --> 00:17:01,020
I'll let you know.

356
00:17:10,812 --> 00:17:13,075
So? Do you like her
for the murder?

357
00:17:13,162 --> 00:17:15,034
[Lisbon]
'No, but I like her.'

358
00:17:15,817 --> 00:17:17,340
What do you got?

359
00:17:17,427 --> 00:17:19,821
Uh, text messages from
the victim's cell phone.

360
00:17:19,908 --> 00:17:22,519
Yoli's cousin said she was
texting while leaving the club.

361
00:17:22,606 --> 00:17:25,914
What was the last text she sent
before she was murdered?

362
00:17:26,001 --> 00:17:27,959
Uh, "on my way.
Open the champagne.

363
00:17:28,047 --> 00:17:30,440
Our favorite hotel?"
sounds personal.

364
00:17:30,527 --> 00:17:32,529
Very personal.
Who's it to?

365
00:17:32,616 --> 00:17:35,576
Uh, prepaid phone.
No record of the owner.

366
00:17:35,663 --> 00:17:38,361
Her cousin might have been mad
about this affair business.

367
00:17:38,448 --> 00:17:40,624
I think we should talk
to her boss again.

368
00:17:41,756 --> 00:17:44,237
[intense music]

369
00:17:47,805 --> 00:17:51,157
Excuse me. We're looking
for Sergeant Henderson's office.

370
00:17:51,244 --> 00:17:53,289
- Towards the back on the left.
- Thanks.

371
00:17:53,376 --> 00:17:54,551
That Yoli's desk there?

372
00:17:54,638 --> 00:17:56,379
Yeah, that's where she sat.

373
00:17:56,466 --> 00:17:57,685
Oh. Thank you.

374
00:17:59,034 --> 00:18:00,818
[Patrick]
I'll catch up with you.

375
00:18:00,905 --> 00:18:02,472
[Lisbon]
'Alright. Don't wander off.'

376
00:18:02,559 --> 00:18:03,647
Wouldn't dream of it.

377
00:18:08,435 --> 00:18:11,046
[intense music]

378
00:18:20,273 --> 00:18:22,318
The text messages started
two weeks ago.

379
00:18:22,405 --> 00:18:24,929
They paint a picture
of a pretty wild affair.

380
00:18:25,016 --> 00:18:27,367
Did you know if Yoli
was romantically involved

381
00:18:27,454 --> 00:18:29,238
with anyone on the job?

382
00:18:29,325 --> 00:18:30,805
I can assure you,
Agent Lisbon

383
00:18:30,892 --> 00:18:33,460
I keep a tight rein
over my undercover officers.

384
00:18:33,547 --> 00:18:36,289
Then how do you explain those
texts? There's pages of them.

385
00:18:36,376 --> 00:18:38,334
These aren't love tweets.
These are gang codes.

386
00:18:38,421 --> 00:18:40,467
Yoli picked this up while
surveilling a gang

387
00:18:40,554 --> 00:18:41,946
a couple months back.
Look--

388
00:18:42,033 --> 00:18:44,688
See that? "champagne"
is cocaine,

389
00:18:44,775 --> 00:18:47,517
uh, "on her way"
is someone's in trouble.

390
00:18:47,604 --> 00:18:49,084
Who uses that code?

391
00:18:49,171 --> 00:18:51,130
Nobody you ever heard of.
The Perry Boys.

392
00:18:51,217 --> 00:18:53,393
A renegade stick-up outfit.
Two brothers and a cousin?

393
00:18:53,480 --> 00:18:55,177
How do you know
about them?

394
00:18:55,264 --> 00:18:58,963
I did some research when I found
out they hit Vega's stash house.

395
00:18:59,050 --> 00:19:00,704
Vega was robbed?

396
00:19:00,791 --> 00:19:03,925
Two days before Yoli's murder.
She didn't tell you about it?

397
00:19:04,012 --> 00:19:06,928
I thought you kept
a tight rein on your people.

398
00:19:07,015 --> 00:19:09,670
Look, nothing in
Yoli's surveillance reports

399
00:19:09,757 --> 00:19:11,106
ever mention the Perrys.

400
00:19:11,193 --> 00:19:13,239
Is it possible
she was working with them--

401
00:19:13,326 --> 00:19:15,110
that's why she didn't
report the robbery?

402
00:19:15,197 --> 00:19:17,199
She wouldn't compromise
her team that way.

403
00:19:17,286 --> 00:19:18,722
Yoli wasn't dirty.

404
00:19:18,809 --> 00:19:20,289
- You sure about that?
- Yeah.

405
00:19:20,376 --> 00:19:22,552
I've one of my people
at her house now

406
00:19:22,639 --> 00:19:24,380
looking for evidence
of an affair.

407
00:19:26,208 --> 00:19:27,601
Van Pelt,
new marching orders--

408
00:19:27,688 --> 00:19:29,646
Find out
if Yoli was on the take

409
00:19:29,733 --> 00:19:32,867
or in contact with a gang
called the Perry Boys.

410
00:19:32,954 --> 00:19:34,129
[clatter]

411
00:19:41,092 --> 00:19:42,398
can I help you?

412
00:19:42,485 --> 00:19:44,748
I'm sorry. I was trying
not to bother you.

413
00:19:44,835 --> 00:19:47,403
But, uh, but since
you asked, yes.

414
00:19:47,490 --> 00:19:48,404
Uh... who's that guy?

415
00:19:51,364 --> 00:19:52,756
That's Trey.

416
00:19:52,843 --> 00:19:56,107
Trey. Is--uh,
a fellow officer?

417
00:19:56,195 --> 00:19:58,632
Yeah, we all came in
the same year.

418
00:19:58,719 --> 00:20:02,157
So you and Yoli
must have been close?

419
00:20:02,244 --> 00:20:05,595
That girl was my heart.
She was always there for me.

420
00:20:05,682 --> 00:20:08,729
My partner seems
to believe that, um

421
00:20:10,121 --> 00:20:12,863
that Yoli was
having an affair.

422
00:20:12,950 --> 00:20:16,215
Nah. Yoli would never
cheat on Lalo.

423
00:20:16,302 --> 00:20:19,783
Her family found condoms
in her pockets more than once.

424
00:20:19,870 --> 00:20:22,003
We all carry 'em.

425
00:20:22,090 --> 00:20:24,005
Never know when you've to
waterproof drug samples

426
00:20:24,092 --> 00:20:26,355
when you're in the field.

427
00:20:26,442 --> 00:20:27,400
Handy to know.

428
00:20:29,097 --> 00:20:31,578
[indistinct chattering on TV]

429
00:20:38,019 --> 00:20:41,414
Alright, mama.
Nap time is now.

430
00:20:41,501 --> 00:20:42,502
Get in bed.

431
00:20:46,593 --> 00:20:48,943
How much longer
is this gonna take?

432
00:20:49,030 --> 00:20:50,640
I don't know.

433
00:20:50,727 --> 00:20:53,687
Tell me what you're looking for.
Maybe I can speed this up.

434
00:20:53,774 --> 00:20:56,167
My kids won't go to sleep
with you here.

435
00:20:56,255 --> 00:20:58,953
I'm sorry, sir,
but I can't discuss the case.

436
00:20:59,040 --> 00:21:01,695
Another Robocop.
Where do they find you people?

437
00:21:05,351 --> 00:21:07,309
These are all family files.

438
00:21:07,396 --> 00:21:09,485
Did Yoli keep
any private records?

439
00:21:09,572 --> 00:21:14,011
Uh, a personal journal
or diary, maybe?

440
00:21:14,098 --> 00:21:15,578
You can check her computer.

441
00:21:15,665 --> 00:21:18,146
We already did, at work
and the laptop at home.

442
00:21:18,233 --> 00:21:20,017
She didn't keep anything
important on those.

443
00:21:21,236 --> 00:21:22,193
Too paranoid.

444
00:21:23,456 --> 00:21:24,935
What computer did she use?

445
00:21:30,245 --> 00:21:32,334
Right there.

446
00:21:32,421 --> 00:21:33,379
Excuse me.

447
00:21:34,641 --> 00:21:36,382
It's okay, Rafi.

448
00:21:36,469 --> 00:21:38,427
The lady needs
to look at the computer.

449
00:21:38,514 --> 00:21:39,907
She won't be here long.

450
00:21:41,387 --> 00:21:42,605
[mouse clicking]

451
00:21:45,086 --> 00:21:47,393
[instrumental music]

452
00:21:53,573 --> 00:21:55,270
She'll be gone
in a few minutes.

453
00:21:55,357 --> 00:21:56,489
[Lalo]
'It's okay.'

454
00:21:59,013 --> 00:22:01,320
[instrumental music]

455
00:22:12,113 --> 00:22:13,027
- 'Van Pelt.'
- Hey, boss.

456
00:22:13,114 --> 00:22:14,985
Did you find anything?

457
00:22:15,072 --> 00:22:18,032
[Grace]
'Yoli uploaded photos of a house
onto her kids' computer'

458
00:22:18,119 --> 00:22:19,729
'the day before the crime.'

459
00:22:19,816 --> 00:22:21,601
The photos link
to a foreclosure site

460
00:22:21,688 --> 00:22:24,734
that show the house has been
vacant for six months.

461
00:22:24,821 --> 00:22:27,607
The perfect place
for the Perrys to hide out.

462
00:22:27,694 --> 00:22:30,000
We're gonna need
that address.

463
00:22:30,087 --> 00:22:32,481
Daddy's home.

464
00:22:32,568 --> 00:22:34,265
Hey! You must be Trey.

465
00:22:34,353 --> 00:22:37,356
Hey. I must be.
Who am I waving at?

466
00:22:37,443 --> 00:22:41,316
I'm one of the CBI people
investigating Yoli's murder.

467
00:22:41,403 --> 00:22:42,709
Yeah? On our couch?

468
00:22:42,796 --> 00:22:44,798
Well, you'd be surprised
what you can learn.

469
00:22:44,885 --> 00:22:47,148
Really? Like what?

470
00:22:47,235 --> 00:22:48,367
Well, this particular couch

471
00:22:48,454 --> 00:22:50,325
it's very comfortable
on the first sit

472
00:22:50,412 --> 00:22:53,372
but, uh, after time, gonna give
your back a lot of grief.

473
00:22:53,459 --> 00:22:55,069
Hey, are you ready to go?

474
00:22:55,156 --> 00:22:56,984
- Where we going?
- Tracking the Perry Boys.

475
00:22:57,071 --> 00:22:59,726
- They may have killed Yoli.
- You want me to come?

476
00:22:59,813 --> 00:23:02,468
- We got extra vests.
- Yeah, probably not my size.

477
00:23:02,555 --> 00:23:04,992
- Why don't you wait here?
- That's great--I'll wait here.

478
00:23:05,079 --> 00:23:06,776
Hold down the fort.
Good luck.

479
00:23:11,302 --> 00:23:13,130
It's a whole new you.

480
00:23:13,217 --> 00:23:17,396
Yeah. Be happy I wasn't
out there as a crackhead today.

481
00:23:17,483 --> 00:23:19,485
Props include
urine-soaked pants.

482
00:23:19,572 --> 00:23:20,529
[Jane]
'Charming.'

483
00:23:22,662 --> 00:23:25,099
Uh, are those props, too?

484
00:23:25,186 --> 00:23:28,276
Drugs? No.
These are the real deal.

485
00:23:28,363 --> 00:23:29,799
I was out doing
hand-to-hands today.

486
00:23:29,886 --> 00:23:31,584
You know, making buys
in different areas

487
00:23:31,671 --> 00:23:33,324
see who
the current sellers are.

488
00:23:33,412 --> 00:23:35,805
That's quite a haul.
Colorful.

489
00:23:35,892 --> 00:23:37,546
What--what do you do
with the goods?

490
00:23:39,983 --> 00:23:42,333
Everything goes
into the property room.

491
00:23:42,421 --> 00:23:45,336
Investigation unit catches you
with as much as a crack pipe

492
00:23:45,424 --> 00:23:47,426
in your car, they come down
pretty hard.

493
00:23:47,513 --> 00:23:49,906
Mm.

494
00:23:49,993 --> 00:23:51,560
Must be difficult
living two lives.

495
00:23:53,388 --> 00:23:56,086
Well, you learn
to compartmentalize.

496
00:23:56,173 --> 00:23:57,784
Mm. How was Yoli with that?

497
00:23:59,438 --> 00:24:01,396
Yoli. God bless her.

498
00:24:01,483 --> 00:24:04,181
She was one of the best,
actually. She had to be.

499
00:24:04,268 --> 00:24:05,966
- You met her family, right?
- Mm-hmm.

500
00:24:06,053 --> 00:24:08,534
Yeah, she was putting that
husband of hers through school.

501
00:24:08,621 --> 00:24:11,493
So Yoli was good,
but, uh, you're better?

502
00:24:13,495 --> 00:24:17,151
So why is it that Yoli got
the, uh, Vega case and not you?

503
00:24:17,238 --> 00:24:18,892
That's--
that's the big case, right?

504
00:24:18,979 --> 00:24:22,548
Well, let's just say the short
dresses didn't hurt Yoli at all.

505
00:24:22,635 --> 00:24:23,940
Tell you one thing, though,

506
00:24:24,027 --> 00:24:26,508
I wouldn't have let Vega's men
do me like that.

507
00:24:26,595 --> 00:24:28,249
You think Vega
had her killed?

508
00:24:28,336 --> 00:24:30,425
[Terry]
'Aw, come on.
She's an undercover cop.'

509
00:24:30,512 --> 00:24:32,296
This guy's
a notorious gangster.

510
00:24:32,383 --> 00:24:35,169
How far have you really
gotta look?

511
00:24:35,256 --> 00:24:36,257
'Sup, trey?

512
00:24:36,344 --> 00:24:37,388
[Trey]
'You got it.'

513
00:24:37,476 --> 00:24:39,042
- Oh.
- Oh, I am so sorry.

514
00:24:39,129 --> 00:24:41,175
I'm sorry. Trey--
oh, that's embarrassing.

515
00:24:41,262 --> 00:24:44,265
Mike, you got a towel,
a napkin or something? Come on.

516
00:24:44,352 --> 00:24:46,136
That's terrible.
My bad.

517
00:24:47,964 --> 00:24:51,098
Wipe that there. Uh, gonna need
another one of these, mike.

518
00:24:51,185 --> 00:24:53,187
Okay, great. Thank you.

519
00:24:54,231 --> 00:24:56,451
So clumsy.
I-I'm sorry.

520
00:24:56,538 --> 00:24:58,845
[car doors close]

521
00:24:58,932 --> 00:25:01,195
we're looking for Warren,
Dwayne, and Russell Perry.

522
00:25:01,282 --> 00:25:02,631
Expect them to be armed.

523
00:25:02,718 --> 00:25:04,633
They're erratic
and extremely dangerous.

524
00:25:10,291 --> 00:25:12,380
- Van Pelt, you take the side.
- Yes, ma'am.

525
00:25:12,467 --> 00:25:15,078
[intense music]

526
00:25:27,700 --> 00:25:29,440
[gunfire]

527
00:25:29,528 --> 00:25:31,225
[man groaning]

528
00:25:31,965 --> 00:25:32,922
Police!

529
00:25:34,358 --> 00:25:36,273
[man grunting]

530
00:25:39,015 --> 00:25:42,453
[man #3]
We didn't come here
to work out. Don't move, kid.

531
00:25:42,541 --> 00:25:44,543
[Lisbon]
Put your hands in the air!

532
00:25:44,630 --> 00:25:46,545
[man grunting]

533
00:25:49,286 --> 00:25:51,158
Uh! Aah!

534
00:25:51,245 --> 00:25:53,508
[intense music]

535
00:25:56,816 --> 00:25:59,253
[voice on TV]
'I did what I had to do'

536
00:25:59,340 --> 00:26:00,428
Clear.

537
00:26:00,515 --> 00:26:02,038
It's definitely
the Perrys.

538
00:26:02,125 --> 00:26:03,300
[Voice on TV]
'I fought.'

539
00:26:06,086 --> 00:26:08,218
[Grace]
'Hey, boss, I got one down
back here!'

540
00:26:10,351 --> 00:26:12,701
[men grunting]

541
00:26:14,660 --> 00:26:16,226
'nobody could help me.'

542
00:26:22,798 --> 00:26:23,756
[door opens]

543
00:26:27,542 --> 00:26:30,023
- Where'd all this come from?
- Mm.

544
00:26:30,110 --> 00:26:31,938
Your friend Wayne
is so sweet.

545
00:26:32,025 --> 00:26:34,244
Now there's a man
who knows how to smile.

546
00:26:34,331 --> 00:26:35,811
Was he in a boy band?

547
00:26:35,898 --> 00:26:38,422
You were right
about Vega.

548
00:26:38,509 --> 00:26:40,207
So my information
was helpful?

549
00:26:40,294 --> 00:26:41,991
No, but it was accurate.

550
00:26:42,078 --> 00:26:43,993
You're free to go.
All charges are dropped.

551
00:26:47,301 --> 00:26:49,390
Thank you, Agent Cho.

552
00:26:50,521 --> 00:26:52,001
Kimball.

553
00:26:52,088 --> 00:26:53,002
You're welcome.

554
00:26:59,661 --> 00:27:01,271
You know..

555
00:27:01,358 --> 00:27:03,056
...you should do something
about your back.

556
00:27:03,143 --> 00:27:04,971
It's nothing.

557
00:27:05,058 --> 00:27:06,363
You're very
invested in this

558
00:27:06,450 --> 00:27:08,801
man-in-an-iron-face
routine, aren't you?

559
00:27:08,888 --> 00:27:11,368
I bet I could make you
cry like a baby.

560
00:27:14,154 --> 00:27:15,111
I'll bet.

561
00:27:16,678 --> 00:27:18,375
There may be hope
for you yet.

562
00:27:19,376 --> 00:27:21,814
[instrumental music]

563
00:27:23,903 --> 00:27:27,558
Sac PD Narco unit just finished
searching the Perry's house.

564
00:27:27,646 --> 00:27:30,431
They found baggies, scales,
drug residue, but no drugs.

565
00:27:30,518 --> 00:27:32,215
Looks like Vega
stole his coke back.

566
00:27:32,302 --> 00:27:35,305
The Perrys let the killer in
the house. Someone they trusted.

567
00:27:35,392 --> 00:27:37,960
Otherwise, Dwayne would've
died with a gun in his hand

568
00:27:38,047 --> 00:27:39,658
instead of
a video game controller.

569
00:27:39,745 --> 00:27:41,268
Did ballistics come back?

570
00:27:41,355 --> 00:27:43,574
Yeah, the .380 casings
found at the Perry house

571
00:27:43,662 --> 00:27:46,360
match those from Yoli's crime
scene, all from the same gun.

572
00:27:46,447 --> 00:27:49,450
ME puts the Perrys' time of
death the same night as Yoli's.

573
00:27:49,537 --> 00:27:51,452
So whoever killed
the Perrys killed Yoli.

574
00:27:51,539 --> 00:27:54,150
Great. We've got no suspects.
We're back to square one.

575
00:27:54,237 --> 00:27:56,413
Well...

576
00:27:56,500 --> 00:27:58,981
I wouldn't say
square one exactly.

577
00:27:59,068 --> 00:28:00,026
No?

578
00:28:01,331 --> 00:28:02,289
No.

579
00:28:03,682 --> 00:28:06,423
[intense music]

580
00:28:12,429 --> 00:28:14,214
Hey, Candide, we're ready.

581
00:28:16,390 --> 00:28:18,784
[intense music]

582
00:28:32,667 --> 00:28:34,364
[whirring]

583
00:28:34,451 --> 00:28:36,062
[door clanks open]

584
00:28:40,196 --> 00:28:42,721
That's quite an impressive
pile you have there.

585
00:28:42,808 --> 00:28:44,287
What are you, uh, doing here?

586
00:28:44,374 --> 00:28:45,506
I'm looking for you.

587
00:28:45,593 --> 00:28:47,682
Well, you can't be
back here.

588
00:28:47,769 --> 00:28:50,032
I can be wherever I wanna be.

589
00:28:50,119 --> 00:28:51,207
Oh. Who says?

590
00:28:52,339 --> 00:28:53,470
The law.

591
00:28:53,557 --> 00:28:54,776
It knows no bounds.

592
00:28:56,865 --> 00:28:58,998
What do you want?

593
00:28:59,085 --> 00:29:00,956
I'm not sure yet.

594
00:29:01,043 --> 00:29:03,306
Glad to see you're having
such a good week.

595
00:29:05,352 --> 00:29:06,527
How much do you want?

596
00:29:07,528 --> 00:29:10,226
Mm... 20.

597
00:29:10,313 --> 00:29:11,271
- Grand?
- Percent.

598
00:29:12,446 --> 00:29:13,490
That--that's insane.

599
00:29:14,448 --> 00:29:17,016
Okay, then. Make it 25.

600
00:29:17,103 --> 00:29:18,539
Get out.

601
00:29:18,626 --> 00:29:19,845
I tell you what--

602
00:29:19,932 --> 00:29:23,065
You tell Omar Vega
I got a deal to make

603
00:29:23,152 --> 00:29:24,763
and we'll call it square.

604
00:29:24,850 --> 00:29:26,939
I told you I don't know
any Vega.

605
00:29:27,026 --> 00:29:28,897
No?

606
00:29:28,984 --> 00:29:31,552
Then why are you
counting his money?

607
00:29:31,639 --> 00:29:34,076
Vega uses this club
to launder his drug money.

608
00:29:34,163 --> 00:29:36,165
It's his club,
that's obvious.

609
00:29:36,252 --> 00:29:37,645
[Jane]
'Look at you.'

610
00:29:37,732 --> 00:29:39,603
You're not a big time
club owner.

611
00:29:41,170 --> 00:29:43,651
You tell Vega there's more
where that came from.

612
00:29:47,089 --> 00:29:48,961
[phone beeps]

613
00:29:50,049 --> 00:29:52,399
[intense music]

614
00:29:56,185 --> 00:29:59,885
That pro seemed like
a piece of work, huh?

615
00:29:59,972 --> 00:30:00,929
Who, Summer?

616
00:30:01,016 --> 00:30:02,626
Oh, she's "Summer" now.

617
00:30:02,713 --> 00:30:04,759
She is summer.
That's her name.

618
00:30:04,846 --> 00:30:06,543
Just like she knows
your name's Wayne.

619
00:30:06,630 --> 00:30:08,415
Look, it was just
some potato chips.

620
00:30:08,502 --> 00:30:09,720
You emptied
the vending machine.

621
00:30:09,808 --> 00:30:10,852
Yeah. She was hungry.

622
00:30:13,333 --> 00:30:14,464
Copy that.

623
00:30:16,989 --> 00:30:18,773
Hi. I was just leaving.

624
00:30:18,860 --> 00:30:20,296
No. You're not.

625
00:30:20,383 --> 00:30:22,559
No? I guess I'm not.

626
00:30:22,646 --> 00:30:25,432
[hip-hopmusic]

627
00:30:25,519 --> 00:30:27,477
we're up.

628
00:30:27,564 --> 00:30:29,871
[music continues]

629
00:30:32,831 --> 00:30:34,702
Whoa!

630
00:30:34,789 --> 00:30:37,400
You mind turning
the bass down a little?

631
00:30:37,487 --> 00:30:39,141
Makes me wanna
go to the bathroom!

632
00:30:42,971 --> 00:30:44,538
You got a signal?

633
00:30:44,625 --> 00:30:45,626
Yeah.

634
00:30:47,758 --> 00:30:49,760
Just give 'em a lead
before you go.

635
00:30:52,241 --> 00:30:53,547
[engine cranks]

636
00:30:56,637 --> 00:30:59,074
[intense music

637
00:31:09,519 --> 00:31:10,520
Straight.

638
00:31:16,439 --> 00:31:17,484
Turn right here.

639
00:31:18,964 --> 00:31:21,140
[music continues]

640
00:31:24,578 --> 00:31:27,189
[Cho]
'I know this neighborhood.
It's derelict.'

641
00:31:27,276 --> 00:31:29,670
It's a perfect place to set up
a drug operation.

642
00:31:31,411 --> 00:31:33,021
[Rigsby]
'Okay, they stopped.
Slow down.'

643
00:31:33,108 --> 00:31:35,632
They're just a few hundred
feet ahead. Let's park here.

644
00:31:38,809 --> 00:31:40,768
How many months
has Sac PD's narco team

645
00:31:40,855 --> 00:31:43,553
been looking for Vega's hideout?
We found it in one day.

646
00:31:45,468 --> 00:31:48,080
[intense music]

647
00:31:50,952 --> 00:31:52,345
I don't see the SUV.

648
00:31:54,216 --> 00:31:57,045
They must have pulled into
one of these warehouses.

649
00:31:57,132 --> 00:31:59,439
Yeah, but where?

650
00:31:59,526 --> 00:32:02,355
Wait a second. Where'd you hide
Jane's tracking device?

651
00:32:02,442 --> 00:32:04,009
His jacket lining.

652
00:32:04,096 --> 00:32:05,097
[exhales]

653
00:32:06,054 --> 00:32:08,274
Jane's jacket and shoes.

654
00:32:08,361 --> 00:32:09,797
We're screwed.

655
00:32:09,884 --> 00:32:10,972
We're fine.

656
00:32:12,365 --> 00:32:13,670
Jane's screwed.

657
00:32:19,807 --> 00:32:21,896
...So I was thinking

658
00:32:21,983 --> 00:32:23,724
it's getting a little
crowded in here.

659
00:32:23,811 --> 00:32:25,682
Walk away.

660
00:32:25,769 --> 00:32:27,249
[Summer groans]
Right now.

661
00:32:30,426 --> 00:32:33,429
If you wanted a date,
all you had to do was ask.

662
00:32:33,516 --> 00:32:35,257
- Where can I find Omar Vega?
- Why?

663
00:32:35,344 --> 00:32:36,824
He's got one of our people.

664
00:32:36,911 --> 00:32:38,347
What makes you think
I know?

665
00:32:38,434 --> 00:32:40,393
You're a hooker.
You had intel on Vega.

666
00:32:40,480 --> 00:32:42,003
You must sleep with his men.

667
00:32:42,090 --> 00:32:43,962
You don't mince
your words, do you?

668
00:32:44,049 --> 00:32:46,573
- I don't have time for this.
- Neither do I.

669
00:32:46,660 --> 00:32:48,618
I just spent an hour
talking to him.

670
00:32:48,705 --> 00:32:49,968
You chased off big money.

671
00:32:50,055 --> 00:32:52,535
Now I have to start
from the beginning.

672
00:32:52,622 --> 00:32:54,189
What the hell
are you doing?

673
00:32:54,276 --> 00:32:55,538
I'm arresting you
for solicitation.

674
00:32:57,453 --> 00:32:58,977
Make sure
you make it tight.

675
00:32:59,064 --> 00:33:01,370
I know how you love
to assert your authority.

676
00:33:01,457 --> 00:33:03,677
What's the matter with you?
A life's at stake.

677
00:33:03,764 --> 00:33:07,072
What is wrong with you?You
think you can come here

678
00:33:07,159 --> 00:33:10,292
and take whatever you want from
me whenever you want it?

679
00:33:10,379 --> 00:33:11,990
You're used
to getting paid. Fine.

680
00:33:12,077 --> 00:33:13,861
How much do you want?

681
00:33:13,948 --> 00:33:15,776
I don't want
your money, Cho.

682
00:33:15,863 --> 00:33:18,083
I was just looking
for a little common courtesy.

683
00:33:23,871 --> 00:33:26,743
Vega's held up at an abandoned
garage on Tenth Street.

684
00:33:26,830 --> 00:33:30,225
Now, take these off of me
and leave me the hell alone.

685
00:33:37,102 --> 00:33:39,147
[handcuffs clicking]

686
00:33:43,108 --> 00:33:45,893
[instrumental music]

687
00:33:49,592 --> 00:33:51,681
A little disappointed
about my shoes.

688
00:33:55,598 --> 00:33:58,601
Is this how
you treat all your guests?

689
00:33:58,688 --> 00:34:01,387
- What do you want to sell me?
- Drugs, of course.

690
00:34:01,474 --> 00:34:05,130
You need a new supplier, or you
might end up shoeless yourself.

691
00:34:05,217 --> 00:34:06,957
Este tontothinks
he's on one, yes?

692
00:34:08,481 --> 00:34:10,787
So, um, this supply--

693
00:34:10,874 --> 00:34:13,486
Where exactly
does it come from?

694
00:34:13,573 --> 00:34:15,966
The narcotics task force
collects information

695
00:34:16,054 --> 00:34:17,533
on every dealer in this city--

696
00:34:17,620 --> 00:34:21,189
Where they operate,
where their stash houses are.

697
00:34:21,276 --> 00:34:23,844
I give you that information
for a fee

698
00:34:23,931 --> 00:34:26,542
and you can re-stock
your supply at will.

699
00:34:26,629 --> 00:34:29,023
[laughs]

700
00:34:29,110 --> 00:34:30,546
How is that amusing?

701
00:34:30,633 --> 00:34:32,983
Oh, it's, um,
it's not funny "ha ha."

702
00:34:33,071 --> 00:34:35,073
it's more funny crazy.

703
00:34:35,160 --> 00:34:38,902
You see, I just got the exact
same offer yesterday.

704
00:34:38,989 --> 00:34:39,990
Mm.

705
00:34:40,078 --> 00:34:41,992
[laughing]

706
00:34:42,080 --> 00:34:45,213
Interesting
negotiating tactic.

707
00:34:45,300 --> 00:34:46,475
I'm gonna call your bluff.

708
00:34:46,562 --> 00:34:47,650
Ah.

709
00:34:48,564 --> 00:34:49,783
You think I'm lying?

710
00:34:49,870 --> 00:34:51,872
There's only one rainmaker.

711
00:34:51,959 --> 00:34:54,353
[sighs]

712
00:34:54,440 --> 00:34:55,832
[clears throat]

713
00:34:55,919 --> 00:34:57,704
Bring her in.

714
00:34:57,791 --> 00:35:00,924
[Bianca]
'What are you doing here?'

715
00:35:01,011 --> 00:35:03,231
Get your hands off me!

716
00:35:03,318 --> 00:35:05,103
Yo! Where's Vega?

717
00:35:05,190 --> 00:35:07,322
I demand to speak to him!
We're business partners!

718
00:35:11,196 --> 00:35:12,893
What's he doing here?

719
00:35:12,980 --> 00:35:14,982
Vega, what are you
doing to me?

720
00:35:15,069 --> 00:35:17,767
I hate to break the news, this
woman's an undercover cop.

721
00:35:17,854 --> 00:35:19,682
Yes, I know exactly what she is.

722
00:35:19,769 --> 00:35:22,729
Actually, she's part of
the same narcotics task force

723
00:35:22,816 --> 00:35:24,774
that you claim
to have access to.

724
00:35:24,861 --> 00:35:26,689
Oh, you're good.

725
00:35:26,776 --> 00:35:29,431
You're very good. She's good.
And you're being set up

726
00:35:29,518 --> 00:35:31,738
for a one-way trip
to the gray bar hotel.

727
00:35:31,825 --> 00:35:33,783
You patted her down
for a wire yet?

728
00:35:33,870 --> 00:35:36,134
Vega, you can't be taking
this guy seriously.

729
00:35:36,221 --> 00:35:39,746
No, to be honest, I don't know
what to make of you two.

730
00:35:39,833 --> 00:35:42,314
I mean, it's not every week
that two dirty cops

731
00:35:42,401 --> 00:35:45,360
show up on my doorstep,
both offering me the same deal.

732
00:35:45,447 --> 00:35:47,232
I mean,
what are the odds, hmm?

733
00:35:47,319 --> 00:35:51,279
Oh, the odds? The odds are
someone's lying. Shoot her now.

734
00:35:51,366 --> 00:35:53,020
Then we'll talk
some business.

735
00:35:53,107 --> 00:35:56,241
Like hell! He's not even a real
cop! This guy's a consultant!

736
00:35:56,328 --> 00:35:58,765
No, you know, I think
that maybe my safest option

737
00:35:58,852 --> 00:36:00,506
is to shoot you both!

738
00:36:00,593 --> 00:36:02,116
Whoa! Wait a minute.

739
00:36:02,203 --> 00:36:04,118
Just wait a minute.
Let's be cool here.

740
00:36:04,205 --> 00:36:05,902
You can't shoot me.

741
00:36:05,989 --> 00:36:10,777
I took out
the Perry Boys for you.

742
00:36:10,864 --> 00:36:13,606
- Ah. Explain.
- They hit your stash house.

743
00:36:13,693 --> 00:36:16,391
I knew where they were hiding
out, so I fixed it.

744
00:36:16,478 --> 00:36:19,699
- As a gesture of goodwill.
- He is lying.

745
00:36:19,786 --> 00:36:23,311
- You weren't there.
- Yes, I was. Ishot them.

746
00:36:23,398 --> 00:36:25,139
That's impossible.
The gun that was used

747
00:36:25,226 --> 00:36:27,402
to kill the Perry Boys
was the same gun

748
00:36:27,489 --> 00:36:29,361
that was used
to shoot Yoli Concepcion.

749
00:36:29,448 --> 00:36:32,233
I know you didn't kill her,
she was your best friend.

750
00:36:32,320 --> 00:36:34,453
Yes, she was.

751
00:36:34,540 --> 00:36:37,717
I loved Yoli. But she
was starting to suspect

752
00:36:37,804 --> 00:36:39,545
that someone
in our unit was dirty.

753
00:36:39,632 --> 00:36:42,809
It was just a matter of time
before she figured it was me.

754
00:36:42,896 --> 00:36:43,984
Yoli was five-o?

755
00:36:45,507 --> 00:36:46,682
Damn.

756
00:36:46,769 --> 00:36:49,381
[Jane]
'That's a touching story.'

757
00:36:49,468 --> 00:36:50,904
There's just
one problem with it.

758
00:36:52,601 --> 00:36:55,256
I killed Yoli,
and I killed the Perry Boys.

759
00:36:57,345 --> 00:36:58,520
I did 'em all.

760
00:37:01,175 --> 00:37:05,353
Eenie meenie miney mo, hmm?

761
00:37:05,440 --> 00:37:07,834
Catch a liar by the toe.

762
00:37:07,921 --> 00:37:10,924
If they holler, let them go.

763
00:37:11,011 --> 00:37:14,014
Eenie meenie miney...mo.

764
00:37:17,931 --> 00:37:20,107
[Rigsby]
CBI! Drop the weapon now!

765
00:37:20,194 --> 00:37:22,631
Everybody face down
on the ground now!

766
00:37:22,718 --> 00:37:23,893
Don't even think about it.

767
00:37:25,504 --> 00:37:26,679
[Rigsby]
'Yoli!'

768
00:37:26,766 --> 00:37:27,767
'Don't move.'

769
00:37:29,334 --> 00:37:30,770
Anyone happen
to see my shoes?

770
00:37:33,120 --> 00:37:36,384
So, you're the one
who helped the Perrys

771
00:37:36,471 --> 00:37:38,299
steal Vega's cocaine.

772
00:37:38,386 --> 00:37:39,692
That's right.

773
00:37:39,779 --> 00:37:41,998
When Yoli suspected
a dirty cop was behind it

774
00:37:42,085 --> 00:37:43,522
why didn't she
come to me?

775
00:37:43,609 --> 00:37:45,045
You're a bureaucrat.

776
00:37:45,132 --> 00:37:46,829
Me and Yoli,
we came up together.

777
00:37:46,916 --> 00:37:49,484
I was the one that sh--

778
00:37:49,571 --> 00:37:51,269
I was the one she trusted most.

779
00:37:51,356 --> 00:37:52,966
Look what it got her.

780
00:37:53,053 --> 00:37:56,230
And you framed the Perry Boys
for Yoli's murder.

781
00:37:56,317 --> 00:37:59,233
That's why you sent her the text
messages in code.

782
00:37:59,320 --> 00:38:02,802
It was easy to get Yoli on that.
I told her if there was

783
00:38:02,889 --> 00:38:05,326
a dirty cop on our team,
we should use code

784
00:38:05,413 --> 00:38:08,198
so we didn't tip 'em off.

785
00:38:08,286 --> 00:38:10,810
[Bianca]  The champagne text meant that I was in trouble.

786
00:38:10,897 --> 00:38:14,814
Once I sent it, I had to wait for her to show up at her car.

787
00:38:15,858 --> 00:38:18,078
[intense music]

788
00:38:21,908 --> 00:38:25,041
You worked so hard to
frame them for Yoli's murder

789
00:38:25,128 --> 00:38:28,088
and then you killed them
with the same gun?

790
00:38:28,175 --> 00:38:30,569
Yeah, that part
wasn't planned.

791
00:38:30,656 --> 00:38:32,875
I went to the Perry's
to split our take.

792
00:38:32,962 --> 00:38:34,442
They wanted to revise
the deal.

793
00:38:34,529 --> 00:38:36,792
Told me I had
to take a reduced cut.

794
00:38:36,879 --> 00:38:39,839
Told me they'd drop dime on me
if I didn't give in.

795
00:38:41,884 --> 00:38:43,538
I didn't give in.

796
00:38:43,625 --> 00:38:45,584
I guess you showed them.

797
00:38:45,671 --> 00:38:47,150
You don't get it.

798
00:38:47,237 --> 00:38:48,717
Suits never do.

799
00:38:48,804 --> 00:38:50,023
Try me.

800
00:38:52,634 --> 00:38:55,637
I been in narcotics
my whole career.

801
00:38:55,724 --> 00:38:57,335
Bustin' punks like the Perrys

802
00:38:57,422 --> 00:39:01,034
that got more money in their
pockets than I make in a year.

803
00:39:01,121 --> 00:39:02,078
It never ends.

804
00:39:03,689 --> 00:39:07,736
So why try to beat 'em
when you can just join 'em?

805
00:39:07,823 --> 00:39:09,738
Well, now you can
join 'em in prison.

806
00:39:18,921 --> 00:39:19,879
Thank you.

807
00:39:21,489 --> 00:39:22,403
hey.

808
00:39:25,014 --> 00:39:26,494
What do you want?

809
00:39:26,581 --> 00:39:27,887
Feeling bad now?

810
00:39:27,974 --> 00:39:30,150
Roughed up
the down-on-her-luck call girl?

811
00:39:30,237 --> 00:39:31,804
Don't worry about me.
I'm fine.

812
00:39:35,460 --> 00:39:36,852
I wanna use you.

813
00:39:36,939 --> 00:39:38,854
Oh, be still
my beating heart.

814
00:39:38,941 --> 00:39:39,942
Yes or no?

815
00:39:41,770 --> 00:39:43,381
Okay.

816
00:39:43,468 --> 00:39:46,993
Don't expect just because you're
a cop, you get a discount.

817
00:39:47,080 --> 00:39:50,039
- Standard rates apply.
- Not for sex.

818
00:39:50,126 --> 00:39:51,780
For information.

819
00:39:51,867 --> 00:39:53,521
I can use a good
confidential informant.

820
00:39:58,657 --> 00:39:59,832
Cash money, right?

821
00:40:01,094 --> 00:40:02,051
Right.

822
00:40:03,139 --> 00:40:05,315
You know, Cho,
I like you.

823
00:40:06,708 --> 00:40:09,668
You got a mysterious,
feline vibe.

824
00:40:09,755 --> 00:40:10,756
Is that a "yes"?

825
00:40:12,235 --> 00:40:14,586
Kimball..

826
00:40:14,673 --> 00:40:16,588
...for cash money,
I'd snitch on my mom.

827
00:40:22,420 --> 00:40:23,421
What'd she do?

828
00:40:27,120 --> 00:40:29,339
You got paper to sign, or what?

829
00:40:31,211 --> 00:40:33,735
[instrumental music]

830
00:40:39,611 --> 00:40:40,612
Oh, hey!

831
00:40:42,440 --> 00:40:45,312
You don't look worse for wear
after your showdown with Vega.

832
00:40:45,399 --> 00:40:47,575
Oh, I'm fine, apart
from a couple of holes

833
00:40:47,662 --> 00:40:49,272
in my socks
from tap dancing.

834
00:40:49,359 --> 00:40:51,318
You were right.
Your offer to Vega helped

835
00:40:51,405 --> 00:40:54,103
flush out the real killer.
How'd you know it was Bianca?

836
00:40:54,190 --> 00:40:55,627
Well, unlike her co-workers

837
00:40:55,714 --> 00:40:58,107
Bianca never took off
her criminal disguise.

838
00:40:58,194 --> 00:40:59,457
So it was a guess.

839
00:40:59,544 --> 00:41:01,589
Ah, you make it
sound so artless.

840
00:41:01,676 --> 00:41:02,677
- It's time.
- For what?

841
00:41:03,896 --> 00:41:05,593
We need to talk
about Red John.

842
00:41:05,680 --> 00:41:07,813
Oh. Grieving widower
at my 12:00.

843
00:41:10,076 --> 00:41:12,208
Your 6:30.

844
00:41:12,295 --> 00:41:14,428
- Agent Lisbon?
- Hi. Can I help you?

845
00:41:14,515 --> 00:41:16,212
I'm looking for
the evidence room.

846
00:41:16,299 --> 00:41:18,258
They're releasing
Yoli's things.

847
00:41:18,345 --> 00:41:19,694
It's downstairs
two levels.

848
00:41:21,957 --> 00:41:23,002
Sir?

849
00:41:25,918 --> 00:41:27,702
Your wife's
undercover assignment

850
00:41:27,789 --> 00:41:29,791
was to help take down
Omar Vega,

851
00:41:29,878 --> 00:41:31,401
a drug dealer wanted
in connection

852
00:41:31,489 --> 00:41:32,490
with multiple murders.

853
00:41:34,056 --> 00:41:36,406
With what we learned
from Yoli

854
00:41:36,494 --> 00:41:38,800
we found Vega's operation
last night

855
00:41:38,887 --> 00:41:41,803
and we arrested him
with 20 pounds of cocaine.

856
00:41:41,890 --> 00:41:44,284
I doubt he'll ever set foot
on the streets again.

857
00:41:46,068 --> 00:41:48,462
Yoli saved
a lot of lives.

858
00:41:48,549 --> 00:41:49,507
Thank you...

859
00:41:50,377 --> 00:41:51,334
I guess.

860
00:42:04,913 --> 00:42:06,915
[theme music]

